  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a tree with NNN vertices, rooted at vertex 111. The iii-th vertex of this tree has the integer AiA_iAi​ written on it.\n\nFor each vertex uuu (1≤u≤N1 \\leq u \\leq N1≤u≤N), find the number of divisors of the product of all AvA_vAv​ such that vvv lies in the subtree of uuu.\n\nFormally, for each uuu:\n\n\nLet SuS_uSu​ denote the set of vertices that lie in the subtree of uuu (including uuu).\nDefine Xu=∏v∈SuAvX_u = \\prod_{v \\in S_u} A_vXu​=∏v∈Su​​Av​\nFind the number of divisors of XuX_uXu​\nThe answer may be large, so report it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains an integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases. The description of the test cases follows.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, the number of vertices.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the values written on the vertices.\nThe next N−1N-1N−1 lines describe the edges of the tree. The iii-th of these N−1N-1N−1 lines contains two space-separated integers uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, denoting an edge between vertices uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output one line containing NNN space-separated integers. The iii-th of these integers is the answer for vertex iii.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤3⋅1041 \\leq N \\leq 3\\cdot 10^41≤N≤3⋅104",
      "1≤Ai≤1061 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^61≤Ai​≤106",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\leq u_i, v_i \\leq N1≤ui​,vi​≤N",
      "The edges given in the input describe a tree.",
      "The sum of NNN across all test cases won't exceed 3⋅1043 \\cdot 10^43⋅104."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
