        "output": "192 2 8 2 \n5 4 3 2 \n1080 12 60 18 3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The answers are as follows:\n\nFor u=2u = 2u=2, Xu=101X_u = 101Xu​=101 which is prime and so has two factors.\nFor u=4u = 4u=4, Xu=103X_u = 103Xu​=103 which is prime and so has two factors.\nFor u=3u = 3u=3, Xu=102X_u = 102Xu​=102 which has 888 factors, namely {1,2,3,6,17,34,51,102}\\{1, 2, 3, 6, 17, 34, 51, 102\\}{1,2,3,6,17,34,51,102}.\nFor u=1u = 1u=1, Xu=106110600X_u = 106110600Xu​=106110600, which has 192192192 factors."
